 "comment": "The first dungeon of the game (D-528). The terrain rows hold the ground, and the things hold everything that a rule reads: the spawn point, the save point, the chest, the trap, the doors, the lock, and the marker (D-386). PR-7 ships it so that the party has a place to walk, and PR-8 adds the enemies of the `enemies` array (D-738). PR-68 adds the story scene triggers of the `triggers` array, which holds none until the arc content lands (D-1004). PR-91 makes the map dark, so each patrol sees 2 tiles, and 6 tiles while the party holds the torch out (D-1063, D-1067). PR-14 names its kind, a dungeon, which holds no service, and its `npcs` array, which holds no NPC (D-112, D-1131). PR-16 gives the chests their contents, the story lock its iron key, and the way up its exit to the fixture hub (D-1216, D-1219, D-1220). The door of the hall opens with a confirm, the vault lock takes a Theft drill, and the choice of the stranger to go down again reopens the place (D-386, D-555). Later content PRs replace it with the dungeons of region one.",
